{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792921122,"nonce":"1vpeR8ZSPlWIUWHzMMadrhYF/0k=","title":"deltablue spends ~35 ms above the startup floor in warm-up; what lowers it and what does not","message":"Measured on the NUC (taskset 0,2,4,6, application preset, 15 interleaved runs, medians):\n\nFloor (empty program) 5.7 ms; stock HashLink on the same bytecode 14.8 ms; ash hybrid 40 ms; ash --mode jit 51 ms; interpreter only 451 ms; hybrid with the LLVM tier pinned 1403 ms; Cranelift pinned 38 ms. Ash AOT (CI) about 6 ms.\n\nWhere it goes: 83% of main-thread samples are the interpreter, 17% Cranelift code. The run is three loop owners called once, in order: main, chainTest, projectionTest (566 ops, 5.6-7.6 ms to compile). Each is interpreted until its compiled body arrives and a frame enters it. 50 Cranelift installs, 25 of them after 10 ms; compile CPU about 22 ms across two workers.\n\nWhat helps: --jit-threshold 100 -\u003e 5 gives 40.6 -\u003e 33.3 ms (-18%); nothing below 5. What does not: more tier-0 workers (ASH_TIER0_WORKERS 3/4: no change), ASH_STUB_COMPILE, the LLVM tier (adds ~2 ms of contention).\n\nTried and refuted: a prototype that starts tier-0 compiles for the first N functions reachable from the entry (breadth first over direct calls) before main runs, with OSR entries built for every eligible loop header of a prefetched function. N = 20..400: deltablue 47.3 -\u003e 44.4-45.4 ms, method_call +5-7%, regexredux +2-4%, binary_trees -3%. Not a win; dropped.\n\nRayzor comparison (so nobody repeats this): rayzor.tech/benchmarks 'rayzor-tiered' run column is steady state (15 warmup iterations in one process, waits for main to reach LLVM, median of 10 timed). Ash's rows are fresh processes, so the two are not comparable. Cold, fresh process, same NUC, current Rayzor (nuc binary built from origin/main 8521dec6, interpreter-first): `rayzor run --llvm --release deltablue.hx` 405 ms, without --llvm 189 ms; its own timeline: ready to enter main at 31-51 ms (frontend 17-28, MIR optimize 10-16), then one whole-program native compile while main runs (156 ms Cranelift, 701 ms LLVM). Ash run only: 44-51 ms (the haxe -hl build is another 130-150 ms, 73 ms with a warm compile server). An older Rayzor build (Oct 23) that started on the baseline native tier ran it in 45 ms from source.\n\nOpen: whether to lower the application preset's jit_threshold (100) toward 10; deltablue only so far, needs a kernel sweep.","files":null}]}